    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That version is much better and definitely fits the tone we need. One more thing—can you add a small section on the potential risks or \"unpredictable errors\" that can happen even with horizontal scaling? I want to acknowledge that while it's more resilient, we still have to watch out for unexpected technical glitches or resource conflicts that might pop up when the system is trying to scale rapidly. Just a brief paragraph on being proactive about those kinds of issues.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While horizontal scaling provides excellent resilience, it's not a complete shield against all technical hiccups. Even with multiple instances, rapid scaling events can sometimes introduce unexpected complexities, such as resource contention or configuration drift across the newly added nodes. It is important to proactively monitor these scaling events, as unforeseen glitches can still occur during rapid provisioning or load balancing adjustments. This vigilance is key to ensuring the system remains stable, even when under extreme pressure.",
      "source": "target",
